# Commercial S10.1 readiness and rollback diagnosis

Date: 2026-09-02

## Scope

This diagnosis covers the failed, public-SFW-only S10.1 activation attempt. It
does not authorize Adult media, AVS, payment, publishing, creator access,
controlled beta or production.

## Observed failure

The canonical S10.1 WMS process reached its ready event, but the one-shot local
health gate was launched in the same second as the `Type=simple` service. Its
first loopback request raced the listener and returned
`S10_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT_RED`, which the controller correctly converted to
`LOCAL_HEALTH_RED` and a fail-closed rollback.

During rollback, the three legacy services were also started as `Type=simple`
units and the external legacy health assertion followed immediately. The
listener was not ready yet, Nginx returned 502, and rollback reported
`LEGACY_PUBLIC_HEALTH_RED`. The legacy processes subsequently became healthy
without another mutation: S7, S8 Telegram, S8 landing and Nginx were active
with zero restarts, and the local legacy health endpoint returned HTTP 200.

DNS was not the cause of this attempt. The controller recorded
`S10_1_WMS_DNS_GREEN` before installation.

## Correction

The controller now waits up to 30 seconds for the exact loopback health
endpoint after starting the WMS listener and after starting the legacy S7
listener. Only then may it run the full health envelope. Exhausting the bound
still fails closed; no second process start or restart is performed.

## Risk and rollback

The change only makes readiness ordering deterministic. It does not weaken any
health assertion, product boundary or credential check. The verified
pre-S10.1 backup at
`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-telegram/20260902T045348Z-pre-s10-1-local-install`
remains the server rollback basis. Reverting this commit restores the previous
controller implementation.
